s in this  case and this is a very rare situation  because of the pandemic  the federal government came in and they  dropped an enhancement  on people in many cases disconnected  from what they were earning  in the job they lost due to the pandemic  so you can always say there are  some people choosing unemployment  insurance instead of working  we don't worry about it because  unemployment insurance  runs out the benefits aren't huge  there's not that many people who even  could earn more  from the unemployment insurance than  from working  uh it's also um uh  just a truth about humans that  people generally want to feel useful and  they want to work so while  sure anecdotally there might be some  people  in normal circumstances that have  figured out a way to earn the same or  almost the same from staying home it's  not really a macroeconomic concern  in this particular moment because of the  enhanced  federal unemployment there are more  people  who theoretically could earn a little  more  from staying home and collecting the  normal state unemployment benefits  plus the enhanced federal benefits then  from going back to the job  that they had that that is theoretically  possible right now and anecdotally it's  happening  so joe biden gave a series of remarks  yesterday on the economy  and talked about how jobs numbers from  april were short of what was expected  and one reason that's being cited is  that because of this enhanced  unemployment  there are more people than usual turning  down jobs  so that they can stay home and collect  that sweet sweet enhanced unemployment  so joe biden says he's going to deal  with that let's take a listen  well look fifth thing we're going to do  we're going to make it clear that anyone  collecting unemployment  who is offered a suitable job must  take the job or lose their unemployment  benefits  there are a few coven 19 related  exceptions  so the people aren't forced to choose  between their basic safety  and a paycheck but otherwise that's the  law  now there are already a ton of things to  talk about here  first of all as joe biden says this is  already the law  all of these unemployment systems in  each state sometimes it's by phone  sometimes it's online there's different  ways that it's done  you regularly have to answer questions  like are you looking for a job  did you apply for jobs have you been  interviewed were you  offered a job that you turned down so  joe biden is not  creating any new law here joe biden is  saying  we're going to enforce the rules on  unemployment  interesting it's really difficult to  enforce  people are self-reporting there's  relatively little confirmation or  oversight there's no central database  where the government could determine  you said you weren't offered any jobs  but you were offered one and you  declined it it's basically the honor  system  uh so this is really just kind of like a  message from joe biden  i don't really know how much will be  done as a result of it but let's listen  to a little bit more  i know there's been a lot of discussion  since friday since friday's report  that people are being paid to stay home  rather than go to work  well we don't see much evidence of that  that  is a major factor  we don't see that that look it's easy to  say  the the line has been because of the  generous unemployment benefits  that it's a major factor in labor  shortages  americans want to work americans want to  work  as my dad used to say a job's about a  lot more than a paycheck  it's about your dignity your place in  the community  being able to look your kid in the eye  and say everything's going to be okay  i think the people who claim americans  won't work even if they find a good and  fair  opportunity underestimate the american  people  so we'll insist that the law is followed  with respect to benefits  but we're not going to turn our backs on  our fellow americans  22 million people lost their jobs in  this pandemic  through no faul